The dual-track share $\theta$. The pre-registered prediction of an interior optimum is not supported: welfare is monotone in $\theta$ and market-track price volatility falls to zero as $\theta\to1$. The welfare spread is of the same order as the seed standard deviation, so the honest reading is 'no detectable interior optimum'. Generated by scripts/paper_tables.py from results/B5. Source: reference_results/ (the Lead's independent reference run; cross-checked against the experiment layer in reference_results/CROSSCHECK.md).
